# For ripgrep, fd and anything else that honours it. Not .gitignore: these
# files belong in the repository and are searched by accident.
#
# `static/vendor/mathjax/tex-svg.js` is one line of 2,108,617 bytes. Any
# repo-wide search matching it prints the whole line, and two of them turned a
# build's ordinary orientation greps -- "how do I create a draft", "does this
# table exist" -- into 2 MB each. That output goes into an agent's context and
# is then re-read on every model call for the rest of the run: it is most of
# why one build cost $42.89 and the next, without them, cost $10.85.
static/vendor/
staticfiles/
# Built copies of the client, which answer every question its source already
# answers, twice.
clients/python/build/
clients/python/dist/
